{"name":"Standing Waters","hex":"#005599","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"standing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of stand"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Erect, not cut down.","Performed from an erect position."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/standing"},{"term":"waters","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of water","Amniotic fluid ."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of water"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waters"}],"entries":[{"title":"Habitat","blocks":[{"text":"In ecology, habitat refers to the array of resources, biotic factors that are present in an area, such as to support the survival and reproduction of a particular species. A species' habitat can be seen as the physical manifestation of its ecological niche. Thus \"habitat\" is a species-specific term, fundamentally different from concepts such as environment or vegetation assemblages, for which the term \"habitat-type\" is more appropriate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Beech_Forest_%28AU%29%2C_Great_Otway_National_Park%2C_Beauchamp_Falls_--_2019_--_1271.jpg/330px-Beech_Forest_%28AU%29%2C_Great_Otway_National_Park%2C_Beauchamp_Falls_--_2019_--_1271.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Habitat"},{"title":"Standing","blocks":[{"text":"Standing, also referred to as orthostasis, is a position in which the body is held in an upright (orthostatic) position and supported only by the feet. Although seemingly static, the body rocks slightly back and forth from the ankle in the sagittal plane, which bisects the body into right and left sides. The sway of quiet standing is often likened to the motion of an inverted pendulum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Yerevan%2C_Armenian_girls_posing_in_photo_shoot%2C_Acting%2C_Posture%2C_Body_language%2C_Armenia.jpg/330px-Yerevan%2C_Armenian_girls_posing_in_photo_shoot%2C_Acting%2C_Posture%2C_Body_language%2C_Armenia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standing"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Rotjan_-_Enderbury_Day_1_-_2nd_half_%2862%29.JPG/500px-Rotjan_-_Enderbury_Day_1_-_2nd_half_%2862%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Rotjan_-_Enderbury_Day_1_-_2nd_half_%2862%29.JPG/1280px-Rotjan_-_Enderbury_Day_1_-_2nd_half_%2862%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Rotjan_-_Enderbury_Day_1_-_2nd_half_%2862%29.JPG/500px-Rotjan_-_Enderbury_Day_1_-_2nd_half_%2862%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This coral reef in the Phoenix Islands Protected Area provides habitat for numerous marine species.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARotjan_-_Enderbury_Day_1_-_2nd_half_(62).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Antarctic_%28js%29_18.jpg/500px-Antarctic_%28js%29_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Antarctic_%28js%29_18.jpg/1280px-Antarctic_%28js%29_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Antarctic_%28js%29_18.jpg/500px-Antarctic_%28js%29_18.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Few creatures make the ice shelves of Antarctica their habitat, but water beneath the ice can provide habitat for multiple species. Animals such as penguins have adapted to live in very col